  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 17 - Decision Inside Another Decision
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_nested_statement
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Decision Inside Another Decision
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'Sometimes one condition is not enough to decide what the robot should
    do.

    A program can place an <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font>
    statement inside another <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font>
    statement. This is called <color=yellow>nesting</color> and allows the robot
    to perform additional checks before executing an action.


    Example:

    <indent=1em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">tile <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#33CC66>scan</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color> tile <color=#D4D4D4>==</color> <color=#CE9178>"WhiteOre"</color>:</font>

    <indent=3em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF">value <color=#D4D4D4>=</color> <color=#33CC66>measure</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font>

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color> value <color=#D4D4D4>></color> <color=#B5CEA8>10</color>:</font>

    <indent=5em><font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>mine</color><color=#D4D4D4>()</color></font></indent></indent></indent>

    The
    second condition is only checked if the first condition is true.


    You can
    also place a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>match</color></font> statement
    inside an <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font> statement,
    or place an <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>if</color></font> statement
    inside a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#D96DD3>match</color></font> case.
    This allows programs to handle more complex situations step by step.'
  isImageBig: 0
